      "content": "#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (std::scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    const std::size_t stride = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    std::vector<int> matrix(stride * stride);\n    for (std::size_t index = 0; index < matrix.size(); ++index) {\n        std::scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[index]);\n    }\n\n    std::vector<long long> columns(stride, 0);\n    for (int row = 0; row < s; ++row) {\n        const int* values = matrix.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(row) * stride;\n        for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n            columns[col] += static_cast<long long>(values[col]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long first_window = 0;\n    for (int col = 0; col < s; ++col) {\n        first_window += columns[col];\n    }\n    long long max_sum = first_window;\n\n    const int last_top = n - s;\n    for (int top = 0; top <= last_top; ++top) {\n        if (top > 0) {\n            const int* exiting = matrix.data()\n                + static_cast<std::size_t>(top - 1) * stride;\n            const int* entering = matrix.data()\n                + static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s - 1) * stride;\n\n            // Keep this contiguous update independent of the horizontal scan.\n            for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n                columns[col] += static_cast<long long>(entering[col])\n                              - static_cast<long long>(exiting[col]);\n            }\n\n            first_window = 0;\n            for (int col = 0; col < s; ++col) {\n                first_window += columns[col];\n            }\n        }\n\n        long long sum = first_window;\n        if (sum > max_sum) max_sum = sum;\n        for (int col = s; col < n; ++col) {\n            sum += columns[col] - columns[col - s];\n            if (sum > max_sum) max_sum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", max_sum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "A serial O(N²) sliding-sum algorithm with contiguous row accesses should outperform the baseline's repeated S-element column traversals.",
  "notes": "No commands or measurements performed. Preserves decimal input/output and initializes the maximum from a complete window, including for all-negative matrices.",
